Contract: `findCause(err) (*HTTPError, bool)` must, given a wrapped error chain, return the first *HTTPError in the chain (via errors.As) and true, or (nil, false) if none is present. Does this implementation meet the contract? If not, name the bug and give the minimal fix.

```go
type HTTPError struct {
    Code int
}

func findCause(err error) (*HTTPError, bool) {
    var target *HTTPError
    if errors.As(err, &target) {
        return target, true
    }
    return nil, false
}
```
